  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "'As soon as' means immediately after. 'By the time' compares two events, often with past perfect: 'By the time I arrived, they had left.' 'No sooner had ... than ...' is a dramatic inverted structure for near-simultaneous events: 'No sooner had I sat down than the phone rang.'",
    "explanation_ko": "'as soon as'는 '~하자마자'라는 뜻입니다. 'by the time'은 두 사건을 비교하며 과거완료와 자주 함께 쓰입니다: 'By the time I arrived, they had left.' 'No sooner had ... than ...'는 거의 동시에 일어난 일을 극적으로 표현하는 도치 구조입니다: 'No sooner had I sat down than the phone rang.'",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "I'll call you as soon as I land.",
        "ko": "도착하자마자 전화할게요."
      },
      {
        "en": "By the time we got there, the show had started.",
        "ko": "우리가 도착했을 때는 공연이 이미 시작된 후였어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "No sooner had I left than it started to rain.",
        "ko": "제가 나서자마자 비가 오기 시작했어요."
      }
    ]
  },
